{"id":"n-20261027-95ykd4","category":"gaming","display_title":"Revisiting Super Mario Sunshine","display_title_he":"בחינה מחדש של סופר מריו סאנשיין","short_summary":"Twenty-four years after its initial GameCube release, Super Mario Sunshine returns on the Switch 2, bringing back its divisive blend of experimental gameplay and tropical charm.","english_level":"C1","words":483,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"Polygon","domain":"polygon.com","url":"https://www.polygon.com/super-mario-sunshine-nintendo-switch-online","title":"24 Years Later, Nintendo's Most Divisive Mario Game Is a Miracle on Switch 2","published_at":"2026-10-27T01:06:52.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-27T01:06:52.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-27T06:31:34.359Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":8,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Back in 2002, Super Mario Sunshine launched for the Nintendo GameCube to widespread critical acclaim. Garnering impressive initial review scores—such as a 9.4 from IGN, a 9.75 from Game Informer, and perfect marks from Nintendo Power—and eventually becoming the third best-selling game on the platform, it initially felt like an unquestionable classic. However, decades later, the 3D platformer has evolved into one of Nintendo's most polarizing releases. Today, players remain sharply divided over the title, with defenders praising its bold creativity and wealth of inventive ideas, while critics point out frustrating camera angles and uneven level designs, including notorious challenges like the Pachinko minigame, to give its apologists a reality check. Now, with the game arriving on the Switch 2 through Nintendo Switch Online's GameCube library, a new generation of players has the opportunity to evaluate it firsthand.","Unlike traditional sequels that simply offered more of the same formula seen in Super Mario 64, Sunshine introduced a radical curveball. Mario was equipped with a water-squirting backpack known as the FLUDD, which served as both a cleaning tool for polluted Isle Delfino and a core traversal mechanism allowing him to hover and rocket boost with the power of water. Traditional power-ups were largely replaced, aside from Yoshi, pushing the game into deeply experimental territory. Rather than following standard platforming layouts, the game functioned like an unpredictable grab bag of unique ideas, ranging from a casino filled with water-controlled slot machines and a rollercoaster boss fight to watermelon-rolling challenges.","While some of these bold design choices failed to land smoothly with everyone, this willingness to embrace the unconventional is precisely what gives the game its enduring character. It established a playful unpredictability, acting as a true predecessor to Super Mario Bros. Wonder where grabbing a Wonder Flower opens a blind box of wild effects. Despite the varied nature of its challenges, the entire adventure remains remarkably cohesive throughout. This unity stems from its immersive tropical island setting, which aesthetically unites every location—from the steel girders of Ricco Harbor to the breezy getaway of Gelato Beach populated by roaming Cataquacks—complete with a distinctive soundtrack featuring ukuleles and steel drums. Unlike other entries that rely on a checklist of disconnected themed worlds, Sunshine succeeds in making its environments feel like an actual, tangible place rather than just a collection of carefully themed levels.","Ultimately, the title embodies the core tourism philosophy of the Mario franchise, casting the player as a tourist on a summer vacation learning the rules of unfamiliar domains in real time, much like exploring the desert world in Super Mario Bros. 3 or journeying through Super Mario Odyssey. Arriving during an era when Nintendo was eager to completely reinvent its beloved franchises—a period that also produced daring titles like The Legend of Zelda: Wind Waker, Metroid Prime, and Donkey Kong Jungle Beat—Super Mario Sunshine occupies a proud, experimental, and unique lineage in gaming history."],"facts":[{"fact":"Super Mario Sunshine originally launched in 2002 for the Nintendo GameCube and became the third best-selling GameCube game.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The game is now available on Nintendo Switch 2 via the Nintendo Switch Online GameCube collection.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Super Mario Sunshine is widely regarded as one of Nintendo's most divisive and experimental games due to its unique mechanics like the FLUDD water backpack and uneven level design.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The game features a cohesive tropical island setting on Isle Delfino with a soundtrack incorporating ukuleles and steel drums.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Back","lemma":"back","pos":"adv","he":"בחזרה","name":"false"},{"text":"in","lemma":"in","pos":"prep","he":"ב־","name":false},{"text":"2002","lemma":"2002","pos":"num","he":"2002","name":"false"},{"text":"Super Mario Sunshine","lemma":"Super Mario Sunshine","pos":"n","he":"סופר מריו סאנשיין","name":"true"},{"text":"launched","lemma":"launch","pos":"v","he":"הושק","name":false},{"text":"for","lemma":"for","pos":"prep","he":"עבור","name":false},{"text":"Nintendo GameCube","lemma":"Nintendo GameCube","pos":"n","he":"נינטנדו גיימקיוב","name":"true"},{"text":"widespread","lemma":"widespread","pos":"adj","he":"רחב היקף","name":false},{"text":"critical","lemma":"critical","pos":"adj","he":"ביקורתי","name":false},{"text":"acclaim","lemma":"acclaim","pos":"n","he":"שבחים","name":false},{"text":"Garnering","lemma":"garner","pos":"v","he":"גריפת","name":"false"},{"text":"impressive","lemma":"impressive","pos":"adj","he":"מרשים","name":false},{"text":"initial","lemma":"initial","pos":"adj","he":"ראשוני","name":false},{"text":"review","lemma":"review","pos":"n","he":"ביקורת","name":false},{"text":"scores","lemma":"score","pos":"n","he":"ציונים","name":false},{"text":"such as","lemma":"such as","pos":"prep","he":"כגון","name":f